    cuisine="Stroopwafels (two thin crisp waffle wafers glued together with warm gooey spiced caramel syrup), Bitterballen (deep-fried crispy breaded spheres filled with rich beef ragout, dipped in sharp mustard - quintessential pub snack), Haring / Hollandse Nieuwe (raw soused Atlantic herring eaten by holding the fish by the tail over your mouth, accompanied by raw diced onions and pickles), Stamppot (comfort food mash of potatoes with kale / Boerenkool, sauerkraut, or carrots and onions / Hutspot, crowned with a juicy smoked Rookworst sausage and a well of rich gravy), Gouda and Edam Cheeses (aged to crystalline perfection), Poffertjes (fluffy miniature yeast-risen pancakes smothered in melting butter and powdered sugar), Kibbeling (deep-fried battered white fish chunks served with garlic remoulade sauce), Erwtensoep / Snert (thick winter split pea soup simmered with pork, celeriac, and sliced rookworst, so thick a spoon stands upright), and Dutch Licorice (Drop - the Dutch consume more salty and sweet black licorice per capita than any nation on Earth).",
    festivals=["King's Day (Koningsdag on April 27 - nationwide street carnival where the entire country wears orange, with citywide flea markets / vrijmarkt and canal flotillas)", "Amsterdam Dance Event (ADE - world's leading electronic music conference and festival)", "International Film Festival Rotterdam (IFFR)", "North Sea Jazz Festival in Rotterdam", "Keukenhof Tulip Festival (March–May)"],
