    worldHeritageSites=["Schokland and Surroundings (1995 - historic island reclaimed from the Zuiderzee)", "Defence Line of Amsterdam (Stelling van Amsterdam) / Dutch Water Defence Lines (1996/2021)", "Mill Network at Kinderdijk-Elshout (1997 - iconic 19 drainage windmills)", "Historic Area of Willemstad, Inner City and Harbour, Curaçao (1997)", "D.F. Wouda Steam Pumping Station (1998 - largest steam-driven pumping station ever built, still operational)", "Droogmakerij de Beemster (Beemster Polder - 1999)", "Rietveld Schröder House (2000)", "Wadden Sea (transboundary)", "Seventeenth-Century Canal Ring Area of Amsterdam inside the Singelgracht (2010)", "Van Nelle Factory in Rotterdam (2014)", "Colonies of Benevolence (2021)", "Eise Eisinga Planetarium in Franeker (2023 - world's oldest working mechanical planetarium, built 1781)"],
