    flagDescription="Horizontal tricolor of three equal bands of red (bright vermilion), white, and blue (cobalt); dating from the 16th century, it is the oldest tricolor flag still in national use and served as the direct inspiration for the Russian and French flags; on royal occasions, a long orange pennant (Oranje wimpel) is flown above the flag representing the House of Orange-Nassau.",
    coatOfArmsDescription="Azure, billetty or, a lion rampant crowned or, armed and langued gules, holding in its dexter paw a raised sword argent and in its sinister paw seven arrows bound together (representing the seven United Provinces of the Dutch Republic); supported by two lions rampant crowned or, draped in an ermine-lined royal mantle beneath the Royal Crown, bearing the motto 'JE MAINTIENDRAI' (I will maintain).",
    symbols={"color": "Orange (Oranje - national color representing the House of Orange-Nassau)", "flower": "Tulip (Tulp)", "animal": "Lion (Nederlandse Leeuw)", "bird": "Black-tailed godwit (Grutto - national bird)", "tree": "Oak tree"},
    landmarks=["Canal Ring of Amsterdam (Prinsengracht, Keizersgracht, Herengracht)", "Rijksmuseum and Van Gogh Museum (Amsterdam)", "Windmills of Kinderdijk", "Keukenhof Gardens (Lisse - 'Garden of Europe' with 7 million blooming tulips)", "Delta Works / Oosterscheldekering Storm Surge Barrier", "Erasmus Bridge and Markthal (Rotterdam)", "Peace Palace (Vredespaleis - seat of the International Court of Justice in The Hague)", "Zaanse Schans Historic Windmill Village", "Anne Frank House (Amsterdam)", "Mauritshuis (The Hague - home of Vermeer's Girl with a Pearl Earring)"],
    travelNotes="Rent a bicycle and glide along the tree-lined 17th-century canals of Amsterdam; admire Rembrandt's 'The Night Watch' at the Rijksmuseum; walk through millions of vibrant blooming tulips at Keukenhof; photograph the 18th-century windmills of Kinderdijk rising over misty polders; taste warm caramel-filled stroopwafels fresh off the iron in a street market.",
    shortSummary="The Netherlands is a visionary seafaring and engineering powerhouse, famed for Amsterdam's UNESCO canals, Keukenhof's vibrant tulip fields, and historic Kinderdijk windmills, crowned by the world's leading semiconductor lithography giant ASML, cycling culture, and masters like Rembrandt and Van Gogh."
